Maintainer action required: this patch cannot be landed by the autonomous agent.

Why: .github/workflows/** is maintainer-managed. The repository-scoped GitHub App
token (ghs_*) has no `workflows` permission, so `git push` of a workflow change
is rejected, and .github/scripts/kilo-controller.sh restores .github/workflows from
origin/main after every session (and excludes those paths from staging). Committing
this change in-tree therefore does not persist; origin/main keeps the failing gates.yml.

Apply (maintainer, with workflow scope):
  git apply patches/0001-gates-workflow-contract-fix.patch
  git commit -am "fix(ci): satisfy gates workflow contract"
  git push origin main

Evidence (2026-11-13, HEAD d542019): with this patch applied,
tests/test_gates_workflow.py -> 7 passed (was 7 failed).

